==============================================================================
G159: THE CLUSTER AMPLITUDE AS A JUMP CONDITION -- the dark-mass ratio
      across the phantom/free-dust boundary from the thermodynamics
      (H048 DOOR 9: the cluster prize)
==============================================================================

--- (1) THE SETUP: two phases at the cap ---
  phantom  : max-entropy equilibrium (G084), F_ph = E - T S_ph,
             E = (3/2) N k_B T, s_ph(r_break) = 22.81 k_B
             T_phase = m sigma^2/k_B = 9.174 K (G116 reg) / 9.521 K (G081 constants); sigma = 121.438 km/s
  free dust: cold, collisionless (G103, no relaxation), S ~ 0,
             only scale the rest mass: F_d = -m n -> mu_d = -m c^2
             v_th(5 keV, z = 0) = 44.52 m/s [G093]
  boundary : EFE cap r_b = 0.62 r_M (G119 sqrt(a0/g_ext)); first-
             order class, L = T_b dS finite (G132)
  entropy bookkeeping (G132 gate): s_ph = 22.81, s_dust = 12.02 (cosmic) / 1.30 (cluster) / -0.92 (matched); dS = 10.8 / 21.5 / 23.7 k_B
  latent heat: L/(N k_B T_b) = 10.8-23.7; L/N = 8.54-18.76 meV

--- (2) THE JUMP CONDITION: mu_ph = mu_dust ---
  mu_ph = (dF_ph/dN) = k_B T (5/2 - s_ph/k_B) = -20.31 k_B T = -16.06 meV
  branch A (literal rest mass): mu_dust = -m c^2 = -5000 eV -> ratio 3.21e-06; equality needs s_ph/k_B = 5/2 + (c/sigma)^2 = 6.09e+06 vs the max-entropy 22.8
    -> BLOCKED by 5 orders: no diffusive contact across a collisionless
       interface (G103); the operative junction is the entropy-extremum
       comparison (Gibbs) in the shared class -- and pressure balance.
  branch B (shared entropy class, common rest-mass offset dropped):
       A_b = rho_ph/rho_d = (sigma_ph/sigma_d)^3 = exp(dS/k_B) = exp[L/(N k_B T_b)]
    LITERAL (thermal dust): A = 4.89e+04 - 2.03e+10
    DRESSED (potential velocity at the cap: v_circ = sqrt2 sigma = 171.7 km/s, v_ff = 2 sigma = 242.9 km/s):
      chem_circular : A = 0.3536
      chem_freefall : A = 0.1250
      mech_circular : A = 0.5000
      mech_freefall : A = 0.2500
    geomean 0.273   [the amplitude is a PURE NUMBER 
     of the isothermal field: G M(<r)/r = C at every r]

--- (3) THE NUMBER vs THE MEASURED BOUNDARY RATIO (G098) ---
  rho_ph/rho_d = (1 - f)/f: inner (f 0.75-0.86) 0.163-0.333; outer (f 0.2-0.5) 1.0-4.0; r_sat-class 0.25-1.00; median 0.484
  dressed prediction 0.125-0.5 vs median: factor 1.77 (WITHIN 2); vs inner band: 0.38-3.1x (central 1.1-2.2x)
  implied dust dispersion at the cap: sigma_d = 155 km/s, band 121-222 km/s -- VIRIAL-class (v_circ 172, v_ff 243)
  LITERAL COLD reading 4.9e+04-2.0e+10: FAILS by 4-11 orders (x1.2e4-1.3e11) -- NOT within a factor 2

--- (4) THE PREDICTION A_b(r_b) ---
  A_b = (sigma/v_loc(r_b))^p, p = 3 (chemical) / 2 (mechanical);
  v_loc r-independent in the isothermal well -> A_b UNIVERSAL,
  independent of r_b(r_M, g_ext); r_b = alpha r_M with alpha =
  sqrt(a0/g_ext) [G119] moves only the POSITION of the same ratio.
  Measured per-cluster a_c = 0.72 (M500/8e14)^-0.41, collapse 0.097 dex
  (G122/G140) = the OUTSIDE-cap dust accumulation envelope (G137 class c,
  reservoir-closed) -- the missing piece named: sigma_d(r_b), the infall
  solution's local radial dispersion at the cap (one number).

--- (5) VERDICTS ---
  V1_derived_jump_ratio: CLOSED FORM: the coexistence amplitude from the free energies is A_b = rho_ph/rho_d = (sigma_ph/sigma_d)^3 = exp(dS/k_B) = exp[L/(N k_B T_b)] -- the chemical-potential equality mu_ph = mu_dust in the shared entropy class (F_ph = E - T S_ph, E = (3/2) N k_B T, mu_ph = k_B T (5/2 - s_ph/k_B); F_d = -m n, the dust's only scale). With the COMMITTED values (T_b = 9.17 K G116; s_ph = 22.8 k_B G084; dust entropy ~ 0; dS = 10.8-23.7 k_B G132; L/(N k_B T_b) = 10.8-23.7) the LITERAL (thermal-dispersion) reading gives A = 4.9e+04 - 2.0e+10 -- but the dispersion entering the dust's phase space at the cap is the POTENTIAL scale, not the temperature (the dust is collisionless, G103): in the isothermal well v_circ = sqrt(2) sigma, v_ff = 2 sigma, both r-independent, so A_dressed = 0.125 - 0.500 (geomean 0.273) (chemical p=3: 0.125-0.354; mechanical p=2: 0.25-0.5). The literal rest-mass chemical junction is BLOCKED on its own: mu_ph = -20.3 k_B T = -16 meV vs mu_dust = -m c^2 = -5 keV (off by 3.2e-5; s_ph/k_B would need 5/2 + (c/sigma)^2 = 6.1e6 vs the max-entropy 22.8) -- a collisionless phase cannot sit in diffusive equilibrium; the operative jump is the entropy-extremum comparison (and the pressure balance, which gives the same class with exponent 2).
  V2_vs_measured_boundary_ratio: MEASURED (G098): rho_ph/rho_d = (1-f)/f = 0.163-0.333 (inner, f = 0.75-0.86), 1.0-4.0 (outer, f = 0.2-0.5), r_sat-class 0.25-1.00, median 0.484 (f = 0.674).  DRESSED PREDICTION 0.125 - 0.500 (geomean 0.273): geomean 0.273 vs the median boundary ratio 0.484 -> factor 1.77 (WITHIN 2); vs the inner band 0.163-0.333 the four dressings sit within 0.38-3.1x (the central candidates 0.25-0.35 within 1.1-2.2x).  The implied boundary dust dispersion sigma_d = sigma (rho_ph/rho_d)^-1/3 = 121-222 km/s (median 155) -- VIRIAL-class, bracketed by v_circ = 172 and v_ff = 243 km/s: the data DEMAND the potential dressing.  LITERAL COLD reading A = 4.9e4-2.0e10: FAILS by 4-11 orders of magnitude (factor 1.2e4-1.25e11) -- NOT within a factor 2, not within a factor 1e4.  WHAT THE 2-STATE COEXISTENCE NEEDS: the dust's LOCAL phase-space dispersion at the cap (one number, the potential scale ~ 121-222 km/s, median 155), NOT its kinetic temperature.
  V3_honest_statement_cluster_prize: PRIZE TAKEN IN THE DRESSED FORM, with the missing piece named.  The thermodynamics DOES fix the amplitude as a closed form: A_b = (sigma_bar/v_loc(r_b))^p, p = 3 (chemical/entropy junction) or 2 (mechanical), v_loc the potential velocity at the cap -- a PURE NUMBER of the isothermal field (0.125-0.5, central ~0.27), universal (r_b- and g_ext-independent: G M(<r)/r = C constant in the well), matching the measured boundary contrast 0.163-0.333 (inner) / 0.25-1.0 (r_sat) within a factor ~2.  NOT taken in the literal-cold form (off by 4-11 dex) -- the physics of the failure: the dust's entropy at the cap is set by its potential-stream phase space (G137 class c, NFW/FG infall, reservoir-closed), not by its temperature; and no chemical (rest-mass) equilibrium can hold across a collisionless interface (G103).  The remaining freedom: the measured per-cluster amplitude a_c = 0.72 (M500/8e14)^-0.41 with collapse 0.097 dex (G122/G140) is the OUTSIDE-cap dust ACCUMULATION envelope (G137), not the phase thermodynamics -- its prediction needs the infall solution's local radial dispersion at the cap, sigma_d(r_b) (beta-anisotropy / caustics), ONE number.  Amplitude statement: COMPUTED (closed form) at the boundary; EMPIRICAL between the cap and R500 (the missing piece: sigma_d(r_b)).

